WEBVTT

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:10.490
This wall is what's keeping this 
town trapped 34 years in the past.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:13.320
But who did this? And why?

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.990
Hey, hang on! There's a movie 
I want to see next week!

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:17.870
Blaze...

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:21.140
Whether or not that'll be 
possible depends on this wall,

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.510
and on whoever put it here.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:26.410
March 29 15:07

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:28.160
The one who made it?

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:29.570
What do you mean?

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:31.880
Doesn't it seem odd to you?

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:32.920
What?

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.130
This strange time wall...

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:41.010
Life in this town seems 
so peaceful at a glance.

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:45.850
But there are numerous Horologues 
in the forest surrounding it.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.790
Now that you mention it...

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:52.880
Thinking back, it's almost as if the 
Horologues are protecting the town.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:55.070
Life for its residents 
is just that peaceful.

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:58.550
You're right. I guess you 
might call that mysterious.

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:00.490
Nothing mysterious about it.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:03.890
It just means those Horologue 
wimps are scared of me.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.770
Are you that stupid?

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:08.580
Why do you think it attacked us 
the moment we entered the forest?

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:11.720
Huh? That was, you know...

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:12.960
Its way of saying hello?

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:17.260
That's what I mean. It's as if the 
Horologues are letting us do as we please,

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:19.710
and observing us every step of the way.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:23.950
And the other thing that's bothering me

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:27.600
is that this town keeps repeating 
the same day for some reason.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:31.110
Huh? You...

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.140
Oh, you're...

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:38.480
So that's why even when we 
saw her the second time,

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.820
she acted like we'd never met before.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:41.530
Yeah.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:44.930
If time really is going backwards,

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:47.540
she wouldn't remember us because 
she hadn't met us yet.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:53.710
If we assume the town's time was 
eaten the moment we entered it,

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:55.070
the pieces fit together.

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:05.300
What do you think of my deduction?

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.810
You're exactly right.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:10.810
That's some sharp intuition you have,

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.310
little brat.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:27.130
We've got nothing against you, 
and we don't want to hurt you,

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:30.160
but now that you've figured out the truth...

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:32.620
We can't let you live.

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:37.670
<i>One of the rings that controls a Horologue?</i>

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.750
So you guys are behind all this?

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:42.260
Sadly, you're wrong there.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:45.000
His Majesty is a busy man.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.010
He won't be going to the 
trouble of coming to see you.

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:52.890
Oh, so you guys just strolled out here 
because your leader told you to?

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:56.650
You see, I'm not a very gutsy guy.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:04.040
His Majesty is a much more frightening 
being than you guys think!

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:11.330
Oh, dear. I forgot to introduce myself.

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:14.000
I'm Fujibayashi Kyosuke.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.830
I thought I'd lured you all here, 
but it looks like one got away.

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:21.590
Still, that'll make this even easier for me.

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:23.630
That's my line!

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:31.080
My name is Raiko.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.440
I bear no grudge against the lot of you,

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:36.020
but if you stand in the way 
of His Majesty's experiment,

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:38.400
I will not hold back.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:42.150
Keep your hands off my little brother!

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:48.230
Who are you?

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:53.440
Hey, Gramps, are you the type that likes 
to let your fists do the talking?

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:56.310
So am I! And I'm the worst villain around!

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:58.710
I'll take you—whoa!

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.040
Hey! Don't dodge me!

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:04.300
<i>He's tougher than I thought.</i>

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:07.820
You three aren't half bad.

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:10.550
Enough talk! Hurry up and face me, old man!

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:13.930
Let's duke it out over there! Come on!

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:22.310
By the way, young lady...

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:24.820
I thought you looked familiar.

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:29.070
It's been twelve years, uh... 
what was your name again?

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:31.110
Let's see now...

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:34.280
Oh! Nana! Little Nana!

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:41.770
<i>Nana? That was Mom's name!</i>

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:44.340
<i>So is Mina really my mother?</i>

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:47.190
<i>But why a fake name?</i>

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:51.560
You were all over Victor back then.

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:55.260
You still look exactly the same, though.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:59.100
Why don't you tell me the secret 
behind your youthful looks?

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:05.820
He's...

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:10.650
Here I come!

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:15.950
Come on, is that all you've got?

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:18.870
And little lady, where's that 
fury you had a moment ago?

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:21.620
Did I say something wrong?

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:31.840
Your attacks are repulsive, old man.

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.200
Isn't my Horologue fast?

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:37.970
And it's got more than speed.
It can extend and contract at will.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:41.960
It's the perfect partner 
for a lazy guy like me.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:44.480
You talk too much!

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:48.980
<i>Calm down. Focus on the 
enemy in front of me first!</i>

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:53.090
I haven't seen you in so long. 
Of course I'm sentimental.

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:55.350
Is the boy with the glasses your son?

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:57.990
What happened to that 
precocious little boy?

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:01.080
He used to cling to you all the time!

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:05.960
Mina!

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:41.200
Oh, it's you.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.420
Is something wrong?

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:03.730
Oh, it's you.

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:06.400
Is something wrong?

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:11.900
Thanks for earlier.

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:14.660
Why?

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:18.370
Why do you suffer?

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:21.430
You saved Eve's life.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:24.410
Why aren't you happy?

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:28.680
Why did you hit Vic?

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:30.090
Why?

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:35.050
I truly can't understand.

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:38.540
Don't be so nosy.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:42.680
Every family has its problems.

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:46.160
Problems? What problems?

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:47.580
What kinds of problems?

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.060
What's the answer to the problem?

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:52.550
Won't you tell me?

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:54.690
What are you talking about?

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:58.220
<i>Who is this guy?
Something's odd about him.</i>

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.710
I finally found you.

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:13.170
I heard His Majesty had ordered you

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:17.420
to come here on a mission, 
so I went looking for you.

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:19.680
Bill... Reidan?

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:24.190
Give me another ring.

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:27.690
I won't disappoint His Majesty this time.

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:29.200
<i>His Majesty?</i>

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:33.990
This time, I will turn 
reality into a video game.

00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:35.940
For my mother.

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:38.230
A game? Your mother?

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:41.250
What do those have to do with one another?

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:42.830
I don't understand.

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:49.020
Allow me to observe your memories.

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:52.080
I want to understand.

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:54.340
Huh? Observe?

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:59.310
Fine. You just want me to tell 
you what happened, right?

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:01.000
I want to make these guys—

00:11:01.880 --> 00:11:05.180
No, there's no need for 
anything so troublesome.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:07.460
I need only eat you, and I'll know.

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:52.080
I see.

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:57.570
He drowned himself in video games to 
avert his eyes from his mother's death.

00:11:57.870 --> 00:12:00.330
Now that I know the course of events,

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:02.420
I still can't understand.

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:05.320
What are you?!

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:11.830
It seems I may never understand 
these creatures known as "humans."

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:13.830
It can't be...

00:12:21.730 --> 00:12:24.190
This is the third time we have met.

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:29.370
You don't remember?

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:31.600
Or don't you recognize me?

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:35.550
Then what if I do this?

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:42.890
You're...

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:48.740
Impossible! Horologues act only on 
their instinct to devour human time!

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:52.640
As Horologues devour vast 
amounts of human time,

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:55.800
they are gradually influenced 
by the humans' memories.

00:12:56.310 --> 00:12:58.470
Eventually, they come to possess an ego.

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:04.340
And my ego disguised itself as a human 
in order to learn more about them.

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:08.180
It is now among the humans, observing them.

00:13:09.690 --> 00:13:13.220
<i>How is it possible? The target 
of my revenge came to me itself,</i>

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:15.140
<i>but I haven't gotten my strength back yet!</i>

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:17.660
<i>And my cards are...</i>

00:13:19.390 --> 00:13:22.030
There are many things I wish to ask you.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:26.280
I have performed experiments over and over,

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:30.490
but I simply cannot 
understand human emotions.

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:31.540
Experiments?

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:33.060
For instance...

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.540
Experiment 1.

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:39.920
The kind-hearted Alex always 
uses his money to help others.

00:13:40.310 --> 00:13:43.490
So I gave him more money than 
he knew what to do with.

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:47.680
But he didn't even make a 
move to take any of it.

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:50.800
He only kept giving his own wealth.

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:53.560
I truly can't understand it.

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:55.560
Experiment 2.

00:13:55.800 --> 00:14:01.190
In another experiment, I pushed Vic 
and Eve into a lake at the same time.

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:04.490
Alexander tried to save them both,

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:07.130
but all three ended up drowning.

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:12.320
I truly can't understand it.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:19.630
What?

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:22.710
You idiot! Watch your back!

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:26.090
He won't think twice about 
using cowardly tricks.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.070
Mina, why...

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:31.140
A mother's love is a remarkable thing.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:33.080
A mother's...

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:35.350
Don't take it the wrong way.

00:14:35.530 --> 00:14:38.450
I did it because my darling 
would be sad if you died.

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:43.110
Remember what I told you?
I don't want to see him sad.

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:47.040
My goodness. The plan was to 
get rid of you two quickly

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:49.990
and then move on to Victor, but...

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:52.270
What are you saying?!

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:53.620
Kiri, go.

00:14:55.180 --> 00:14:57.620
You're the only one who can save my darling.

00:14:58.600 --> 00:15:00.870
Go! Hurry!

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:15.510
It is clearly true that heroics 
spring from the young.

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:18.390
How impressive that you prove 
an equal match for me.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:20.070
Don't make me laugh.

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:24.820
You think that little mosquito-bite 
punch will work on me?

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:26.910
Don't make me laugh!

00:15:30.920 --> 00:15:33.210
In order to repay His Majesty's kindness,

00:15:33.210 --> 00:15:36.120
I must defeat all of you.

00:15:36.420 --> 00:15:40.620
Now I'm gonna show you just how bad I am!

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:51.890
There is no need to worry.

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:55.520
Once my experiment is over,
I will return the flow of time.

00:15:55.520 --> 00:15:57.920
They will come back to life 
as if nothing happened.

00:15:58.990 --> 00:16:02.540
The power to consume time affords 
great freedom in its use.

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:05.270
I can repeat my experiments infinitely.

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:09.400
Now, let me tell you about some 
more experiments of mine...

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:11.650
Experiment 3.

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:15.160
I killed Eve in front of Vic.

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:19.540
Little Vic is normally so calm 
and outwardly emotionless,

00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:23.060
but he showed an anguished expression then.

00:16:24.280 --> 00:16:26.150
Do you not find it strange?

00:16:26.640 --> 00:16:30.550
I killed the mother he 
saw as such a nuisance,

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:32.420
so why was he not happy?

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:33.930
Experiment 4.

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:36.320
Driven by curiosity,

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:39.680
I killed both Eve and Alexander.

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:44.190
I thought, perhaps, killing only 
Eve was not enough to please him.

00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:49.170
But on the contrary,
Vic was even more distraught.

00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:52.250
Is that not strange?

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:54.000
Shut up.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:56.330
Then there was... Ah, yes.

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:59.390
Eve's brush with death today 
was also an experiment.

00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:00.420
Stop it!

00:17:00.420 --> 00:17:04.840
I don't understand why you look so mournful,

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:06.290
even though you saved your mother.

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:09.040
And why did you hit Vic?

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:10.800
That's enough!

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:12.300
Then tell me.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:15.300
What makes you suffer so?

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:16.050
Shut up!

00:17:16.460 --> 00:17:20.310
Not only did you take my memories,
but you toyed with my family's lives!

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:21.810
I won't forgive that!

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:21.640
<b>Speed Up</b>

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:31.340
Do not attack me with your emotions.

00:17:31.830 --> 00:17:34.820
I did not come here to fight you.

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:36.890
He stopped my fastest attack,

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:40.830
Sped Up three thousand times,
with one hand?!

00:17:41.270 --> 00:17:47.080
If my use of the people you care about 
in my experiments displeases you,

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:51.650
then why don't you serve as the 
subject of my experiments?

00:18:05.720 --> 00:18:06.890
Can you see it?

00:18:07.300 --> 00:18:10.170
This is the organ I use to eat.

00:18:10.170 --> 00:18:11.980
As you and your friends guessed,

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:15.350
I have been eating this town's time.

00:18:16.130 --> 00:18:17.860
If I may complain a bit,

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:23.200
the amount of time here is so 
vast that it's all I can do

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:25.010
not to spit it up.

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:29.540
Eating such a large amount 
drains my strength, as well.

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:35.500
At present, I can only use about thirty 
to forty percent of my strength.

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:37.490
If you used your power to the fullest,

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:40.560
perhaps you could damage my eating organ

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:44.240
and force me to spit up the time I've eaten.

00:18:46.150 --> 00:18:47.320
That's the way.

00:18:47.320 --> 00:18:51.940
That expression tells me you 
understand my intentions.

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:55.160
If I spit up all that time,

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:58.340
this town will return to the present.

00:18:58.340 --> 00:19:00.150
But at the same time,

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:04.690
you will never see your dead parents again.

00:19:09.390 --> 00:19:11.060
This is a very simple experiment.

00:19:11.060 --> 00:19:14.710
All you must do is choose 
one of two options.

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:16.920
The first option

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:20.970
is to keep things as they are and 
continue to enjoy your happy family.

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:22.890
The second option

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:25.650
is to uphold your conviction 
as a Chronos Ruler,

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:28.980
defeat me, and return everything to normal.

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:31.220
How truly fascinating.

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:35.380
Victor Putin, the very man who has always 
said time doesn't flow backwards

00:19:35.380 --> 00:19:37.540
and that one mustn't be 
overtaken by regret...

00:19:37.540 --> 00:19:40.440
What choice will he make?

00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:44.370
I will be patiently observing this.

00:19:49.590 --> 00:19:52.210
Your brother is no longer in this world,

00:19:52.610 --> 00:19:56.050
but you haven't lost the memories of 
the time you had with him, have you?

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:54.460
Memories of Your Time

00:19:56.340 --> 00:20:00.360
That means your mother can live 
forever inside your heart.

00:19:57.920 --> 00:19:58.340
Inside Your Heart

00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:03.160
<i>Koyuki... Bill...</i>

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:05.240
Pull yourself together!

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:08.000
You're the only one who can save Eve!

00:20:06.310 --> 00:20:06.720
You're the Only One

00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:09.330
Dad...

00:20:09.940 --> 00:20:15.820
I'm very proud that Vic has grown 
to be such an independent boy.

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:12.690
An Independent Boy

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:18.170
Mom...

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:23.490
Which will you choose? Give me your answer.

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:24.870
You shouldn't have to ask!

00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:26.990
I won't let you toy with my parents again!

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:26.580
<b>Speed Up</b>

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:33.000
And I will be taking back my memories!

00:20:33.420 --> 00:20:35.750
I understand a Chronos Ruler's ability

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:38.500
is proportionate to the 
strength of his will.

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:44.560
It appears you still harbor 
some doubt in your heart.

00:20:52.970 --> 00:20:54.770
Now, this is a fine sight!

00:20:58.130 --> 00:21:04.030
You didn't want your son to 
hear me say any more, did you?

00:21:04.310 --> 00:21:05.700
So what?

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:09.030
If you keep spouting nonsense,

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:12.140
I'll shut your mouth forever.

00:21:19.520 --> 00:21:22.300
What's the matter? Are you done already?

00:21:22.620 --> 00:21:24.920
You do give up quickly.

00:21:26.150 --> 00:21:30.130
Goodness... You disappoint me.

00:21:37.130 --> 00:21:39.690
I can't believe you're my father.

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:41.940
Kiri?

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:48.110
It's so pathetic, I could cry.

